From e2f961409e652c15360ba310e5b13fa0fcc1300a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marko Maksimovic <reaktansa@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:53:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ath79: add support for ASUS RT-AC55U

Specifications:
- SoC: Qualcomm Atheros QCA9558
- RAM: 128 MiB DDR2
- Flash: 128 MiB NAND (Winbond W29N01GV)
- Ethernet: 5x 1GbE (AR8337), WAN on eth0 (RGMII), LAN on eth1 (SGMII)
- WiFi 2.4 GHz: QCA9558 WMAC, 2x2 802.11n
- WiFi 5 GHz: QCA9882, 2x2 802.11ac
- USB: 1x USB 3.0 (Etron EJ168), 1x USB 2.0
- Buttons: reset, WPS
- LEDs: power, WPS, LAN, WAN (blue/red), 2.4 GHz, 5 GHz, USB 2.0, USB 3.0
- Serial: 115200 8N1

Flash layout:
The ASUS bootloader enforces its UBI layout on every boot: the "linux"
volume is recreated if smaller than 0x3013000 bytes, it is restored from
"linux2" if its checksum fails, and missing "lsdk"/"jffs2" volumes are
recreated if free space is available. OpenWrt therefore updates the kernel
in "linux" in place, keeps "linux2" as fallback image and gives the rest
of the space to "rootfs" and "rootfs_data". Calibration data and MAC
addresses are read from the "Factory" UBI volume.

Installation:
1. Upload the initramfs-factory.trx in the stock web UI
   (Administration -> Firmware Upgrade).
2. Flash the sysupgrade.bin from the running OpenWrt initramfs.

Revert to stock:
sysupgrade -F -n <official ASUS firmware .trx>

Signed-off-by: Marko Maksimovic <reaktansa@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
